Eris for Lua 5.3, with strict project heap snapshots

Source: https://github.com/Panakotta00/eris
Commit: 9d328c612a825ca10f1c495595acd96f27f5e288 (master-lua5.3)
Original hashes and local changes: provenance.json. MIT license: LICENSE.

Local format W53 revision 1 rejects upstream ERIS and different ABI layouts;
there is no compatibility migration. C continuation context is explicitly
int64_t. Continuation payload is retained for zero-status C frames as well as
other non-base frames. The base_ci sentinel alone has no frame payload.

Eris serializes Lua object graphs, closure upvalues and suspended Lua stacks.
Native functions and private standard-library continuations need explicit
permanent identities. Host userdata needs a typed persistence constructor;
raw process pointers are not a world-save codec. Hooks and external host state
are not implicitly preserved. The game integration owns those contracts.
